cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite the accompanying paper."
title: "RLmalloc: A DQN-Based Hybrid Decision Framework for Dynamic Memory Allocation"
authors:
  - family-names: Yang
    given-names: Sicheng
    affiliation: "School of Computer Science and Engineering, Sun Yat-sen University"
  - family-names: Ma
    given-names: Jing
    affiliation: "School of Automation and Electrical Engineering, University of Jinan"
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/example/RLmalloc"
abstract: >-
  A faithful re-implementation of a DQN-based hybrid decision framework for
  dynamic memory allocation. The agent selects among a small candidate block
  set pre-filtered by a First-Fit-style rule, guided by an HHI-based reward.
keywords:
  - reinforcement learning
  - DQN
  - dynamic memory allocation
  - fragmentation
  - Herfindahl-Hirschman Index
